8. Earth Application

Earth represents the most mature test environment. Existing weather infrastructure provides large quantities of atmospheric observations. PIEP could integrate:

\text{Weather Radar} + \text{MWR} + \text{Hyperspectral MW} + \text{Satellite} + \text{Lidar} + \text{GNSS-RO} + \text{Surface Stations} + \text{Aircraft} + \text{Numerical Models}.

The important research question is not whether fusion is possible—DestinE demonstrates that it is—but whether PIEP's explicit identifiability formalism, uncertainty calibration, and decision interface provide measurable advantages over existing operational systems. This must be demonstrated experimentally through the OSSE framework described in Section 13.

