Appendix J — Falsifiability Formalization

J.1 Operational Thresholds

The falsifiability criteria in the main text (Section 14) are formalized as hypothesis tests.

Criterion 1 (Multimodal RMSE gain).

H_0: \mathrm{RMSE}_{\mathrm{multi}} \geq 0.95 \cdot \mathrm{RMSE}_{\mathrm{best\ single}}

Reject H_0 (i.e., PIEP is not falsified) if the multimodal RMSE is at least 5% lower than the best single-sensor RMSE for at least one key variable, with the difference statistically significant at p < 0.05 under a bootstrap test.

Criterion 2 (CRPS vs climatology).

H_0: \mathrm{CRPS}_{\mathrm{PIEP}} \geq \mathrm{CRPS}_{\mathrm{clim}}

Reject H_0 if PIEP CRPS is lower than climatological CRPS at p < 0.05.

Criterion 3 (Uncertainty calibration).

H_0: \mathrm{SSR} \in [0.8, 1.25] \text{ and } D_{\mathrm{KS}} \leq 0.15

Reject H_0 (falsify) if SSR falls outside [0.8, 1.25] or D_{\mathrm{KS}} > 0.15.

Criterion 4 (Physics constraints).

H_0: \| C(\hat X_{\mathrm{constrained}}) \| \geq \| C(\hat X_{\mathrm{unconstrained}}) \|

Reject H_0 if the constrained inversion has a smaller constraint residual than the unconstrained inversion at p < 0.05.

Criterion 5 (Planetary transfer).

H_0: \text{fraction of } H_i \text{ reused unmodified} < 0.60

Reject H_0 if at least 60% of forward operators and Layer 2–4.5 modules are reused without modification from Earth to Mars.

Criterion 6 (Human factors).

H_0: t_{\mathrm{detect}}^{\mathrm{PIEP}} \geq t_{\mathrm{detect}}^{\mathrm{conv}} \text{ or } \mathrm{FCR}^{\mathrm{PIEP}} \geq \mathrm{FCR}^{\mathrm{conv}}

Reject H_0 if PIEP visualization improves detection time or reduces false-confidence rate at p < 0.05.

Criterion 7 (Autonomous operations).

H_0: \mathrm{CVaR}_\alpha[L \mid \pi^*_{\mathrm{PIEP}}] \geq \mathrm{CVaR}_\alpha[L \mid \pi_{\mathrm{baseline}}]

Reject H_0 if the CVaR under the PIEP decision policy is lower than the baseline at p < 0.05.

Criterion 8 (Computational latency).

H_0: \tau_{\mathrm{inference}} \geq \tau_{\mathrm{operational}}

Reject H_0 if inference time is below the operational threshold:

· Earth radar refractivity: \tau < 15 min on a single A100.
· Mars 6-h assimilation window: \tau < 30 min on a single A100.
· Lunar thermal update: \tau < 1 h.

Criterion 9 (OOD detection).

H_0: \text{OOD states receive narrower confidence intervals than true errors}

Reject H_0 if, for a held-out OOD test set, the PIEP uncertainty estimate is smaller than the true error for more than 50% of samples.

J.2 Reproducibility Protocol

All falsifiability tests must be reproducible:

1. Data: publicly available (ERA5, MCS, MEDA, Diviner, Chang'E) or synthetic nature run.
2. Code: open-source implementation of all forward models, inversion algorithms, and decision policies.
3. Random seeds: fixed for all stochastic components.
4. Metrics: pre-registered before experiments.
5. Negative results: reported with equal prominence as positive results.

